[b]◈ THE VILLAGE HEAD'S HALL[/b]
*line_break
You step up to the oak counter. "Daven Marsh hired me to clear whatever killed his bull in the south sinkholes," you tell Bram Tallow. "You grazed forty head out there for twenty years. What lives down there?"

Bram lets out a slow grunt and sets his chalk down. "No love lost between me and Marsh, but I won't let a killer beast sit half a mile from our pens either. That pasture sits over old collapsed limestone pits. Years back, a big armored burrower came up out of those cracks during a wet autumn."

He taps his ash stick twice against the stone floor. "Thick brown shell across its back, huge hooked jaws, spits burning green bile if you let it square up on you. Worst trick is how it hunts. It waits underground and feels heavy boots or hooves thumping through the dirt, then bursts straight up under your feet. Stand on bare white rock or toss a heavy stone to the far side of the grass first, and you'll force it up where you want it."
