[b]◈ THE YOKE & HORN: UPSTAIRS[/b]
*line_break
Downstairs in the common room, bone dice rattle loud against the oak table. Daven Marsh's voice booms up through the floor planks, bragging over a lucky throw while another cattleman groans.

At the far end of the narrow loft landing, you knock once on the end door. It opens almost at once.

Vera stands inside in a loose cream linen shift, dark hair down over her bare shoulders, a tallow candle burning on the washstand behind her. A pair of Daven's polished riding boots sit neatly under the window, and his silver hip flask rests on the wooden chest beside the bed.

"Right on time," Vera murmurs, catching your wrist and pulling you inside before sliding the wooden latch home. "He's three mugs deep and losing track of his silver. We have at least an hour before he even remembers I exist."

She presses her back against the timber door, dark eyes bright in the candlelight, looking up at you with a wicked smile. "Come here, ${name}. Let's put his bed to better use than he ever does."

